  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226611/assets/ce59a60a1e32b0e7e98345d68a8267f1a89fbd49184fbe8e496ce08c6984263d.png)\n\nA company produces bicycles. The scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the number of bicycles made and the company's profit (in thousands of dollars).\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate regression model for this data?",
  "worked_solution": "As values of $x$ increase, the corresponding values of $y$ first increase and then decrease. It seems like the points on the plot are scattered along a parabola, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226611/assets/20acefe1f03a1ba3dd7154eb0ec9ab462009ed1153d7edb282807fac57130328.png)\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the most appropriate regression model is *quadratic.*",
